set_row('F-57', '''        <tr><td><span id="F-57"></span>F-57</td><td>Observation</td><td>The feed is <strong>not</strong> empty. "Zero real alerts" was true of the sample taken at 19:32 UTC on 2026-11-20 and stopped being true twenty minutes later, when one contract produced 99 rows. <strong>Current state (2026-11-21, after the one-swing-per-ticker fix):</strong> the published feed holds <strong>31</strong> alert rows — 12 for <code>KXPRESNOMD-28-AKLO</code> and 19 for <code>KXBTCY-27JAN0100-B97500</code> — and 0 resolutions, because no followed contract has settled yet. The feeds still show an empty state rather than seeded example alerts when nothing has moved, and the threshold, detection and rendering are covered by automated tests so the mechanism is proven independently of whether the demo happens to move. See <a href="#F-61">F-61</a> for the flood and <a href="#F-63">F-63</a> for the resolutions.</td><td>Live alert feeds</td><td><a href="data/live/feed.json">data/live/feed.json</a> · <a href="docs/ALERTS.md">docs/ALERTS.md</a></td><td><span class="badge neutral">Documented</span></td></tr>''')

